        "id": 1952030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-13T22:26:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, both have issues, this seemed marginally better. The addition overflows when the time is nearly at uint64_t max, vs the subtraction which underflows if last_flush \u003e timestamp. The latter seems slightly more likely, e.g. with timestamps and writes from different threads.",
      "parentUuid": "c72cbdd2_d6ded5d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 6,
